  "title": "built-in scenario id/1",
  "description": "A built-in scenario, named the way a share link (s), a lesson's setup, a course pack's scenario item, an investigation pack and an experiment name one. Its id: lower case, words joined by hyphens, permanent once shipped, and a key of SCENARIO_INFO in js/data/scenarioInfo.js and of SCENARIO_PRESETS in js/scenarios.js. A title is a translation of the id (scenario.<id>.title in the catalogs) and never a key. Until Roadmap II Prompt 63 a scenario was keyed by its English name; those names are the second branch, which every reader still accepts through scenarioId() and which nothing new writes. A version-2 world link carries an id; a version-1 link carries a name. FORMATS.md lists it.",
